<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <record id="res_config_settings_view_form_auto_webp" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">res.config.settings.view.form.auto.webp</field>
        <field name="model">res.config.settings</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="base.res_config_settings_view_form"/>
        <field name="priority" eval="90"/>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//form" position="inside">
                <app data-string="Auto WebP" string="Auto WebP" name="dwo_website_auto_webp"
                     groups="website.group_website_designer">
                <block title="Auto WebP Image Conversion" name="auto_webp_settings">
                    <setting string="Auto WebP Conversion"
                             help="Automatically convert /web/image responses to WebP for browsers that support it. Reduces image size by 25–35%.">
                        <field name="auto_webp"/>
                    </setting>
                    <setting string="WebP Quality (1–100)"
                             help="Higher = better quality, larger file. Lower = smaller file, more compression. Default: 85."
                             invisible="not auto_webp">
                        <field name="webp_quality" style="width:80px;"/>
                        <span class="text-muted ms-2">
                            (1 = smallest · 85 = default · 100 = best quality)
                        </span>
                        <button string="Clear WebP Cache"
                                name="action_clear_webp_cache"
                                type="object"
                                class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm ms-3"
                                confirm="This will remove all cached WebP images for this website. They will be re-converted on the next request. Continue?"
                                invisible="not auto_webp"/>
                    </setting>
                </block>
                <block title="Test Install and Config" name="auto_webp_test">
                    <setting string="Python WebP Support"
                             help="Run Python in the Odoo server: import Pillow and encode a test image to WebP. Success means Pillow has the WebP encoder.">
                        <button string="Test Python Import"
                                name="action_test_python_webp"
                                type="object"
                                class="btn btn-primary btn-sm"/>
                    </setting>
                    <setting string="Website Image Test"
                             help="Load a /web/image URL of this website with Accept: image/webp. Success means the response is a WebP image."
                             invisible="not auto_webp">
                        <button string="Test WebP Image"
                                name="action_test_webp"
                                type="object"
                                class="btn btn-primary btn-sm"/>
                    </setting>
                </block>
                <block title="Installation Guide" name="auto_webp_install_guide">
                    <div class="col-12 o_setting_box px-3">
                        <p>
                            This module requires <strong>Pillow with WebP encoder (libwebp)</strong> on the Odoo server.
                            Always install using the <strong>exact Python that runs Odoo</strong> (venv or system), then restart Odoo.
                        </p>
                        <ul class="nav nav-tabs" role="tablist">
                            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                                <a class="nav-link active" href="#webp_tab_linux" data-bs-toggle="tab" role="tab">Linux</a>
                            </li>
                            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                                <a class="nav-link" href="#webp_tab_docker" data-bs-toggle="tab" role="tab">Docker</a>
                            </li>
                            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                                <a class="nav-link" href="#webp_tab_windows" data-bs-toggle="tab" role="tab">Windows</a>
                            </li>
                            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                                <a class="nav-link" href="#webp_tab_macos_intel" data-bs-toggle="tab" role="tab">macOS (Intel)</a>
                            </li>
                            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                                <a class="nav-link" href="#webp_tab_macos_arm" data-bs-toggle="tab" role="tab">macOS (Apple Silicon)</a>
                            </li>
                            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                                <a class="nav-link" href="#webp_tab_verify" data-bs-toggle="tab" role="tab">Verify</a>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                        <div class="tab-content">
                            <div class="tab-pane fade show active pt-3" id="webp_tab_linux" role="tabpanel">
<p>Find the Python Odoo uses, install libwebp, then reinstall Pillow with that exact Python.</p>
<pre class="bg-100 p-2 border rounded">systemctl cat odoo | grep ExecStart   # find the Python Odoo uses
sudo apt install -y libwebp-dev
sudo /path/to/python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
sudo /path/to/python3 -m pip install --force-reinstall "Pillow&gt;=10.0.1"
sudo systemctl restart odoo</pre>
<p class="text-muted">
    If pip reports <code>externally-managed-environment</code>, add <code>--break-system-packages</code>.
    Avoid <code>--no-binary Pillow</code> on Linux; the prebuilt wheel already includes WebP.
</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tab-pane fade pt-3" id="webp_tab_docker" role="tabpanel">
<p>Add to the Odoo image's Dockerfile, then rebuild the image and restart the container.</p>
<pre class="bg-100 p-2 border rounded">RUN apt-get update &amp;&amp; apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libwebp-dev \
    &amp;&amp; pip3 install --force-reinstall "Pillow&gt;=10.0.1"</pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tab-pane fade pt-3" id="webp_tab_windows" role="tabpanel">
<p>The official Pillow wheel for Windows already includes WebP.</p>
<pre class="bg-100 p-2 border rounded">pip install --upgrade Pillow</pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tab-pane fade pt-3" id="webp_tab_macos_intel" role="tabpanel">

<pre class="bg-100 p-2 border rounded">brew install webp
/path/to/venv/bin/pip install --force-reinstall --no-cache-dir --no-binary Pillow Pillow</pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tab-pane fade pt-3" id="webp_tab_macos_arm" role="tabpanel">
<p>Homebrew on Apple Silicon lives in <code>/opt/homebrew/</code>. Library paths must be set explicitly, otherwise Pillow is built without WebP.</p>
<pre class="bg-100 p-2 border rounded">brew install webp
LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/lib" CPPFLAGS="-I/opt/homebrew/include" \
  /path/to/venv/bin/pip install --force-reinstall --no-cache-dir --no-binary Pillow Pillow</pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="tab-pane fade pt-3" id="webp_tab_verify" role="tabpanel">
<p>Run with the same Python/venv as Odoo, then restart Odoo.</p>
<pre class="bg-100 p-2 border rounded">python -c "from PIL import Image; import io; img=Image.new('RGB',(1,1)); out=io.BytesIO(); img.save(out,format='WEBP'); print('OK, bytes:', len(out.getvalue()))"
# Expected: OK, bytes: 44</pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </block>
                </app>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
